|note_res_ELTH=Tottenham Hotspur qualified for the Champions League league phase as the [[2024–25 UEFA Europa League]] winners.
|note_res_ELLS=Initially, Crystal Palace qualified for the Europa League league phase as the [[2024–25 FA Cup]] winners. However, due to [[Multi-club ownership (association football)|multi-club ownership]] rules, they were not permitted to enter the Europa League and entered the Conference League play-off round instead, with 7th-placed Nottingham Forest taking their place in the Europa League.<ref name="CRY_MultiClub">{{Cite web |date=2025-07-11 |title=Crystal Palace set to be replaced by Nottingham Forest in Europa League |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/ckg5260zzp2o |access-date=2025-07-11 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><!-- deliberately repeated references to support transclusion --> Crystal Palace appealed the decision but this was ultimately rejected.<ref name="CRY_Appeal">{{Cite web |date=2025-07-22 |title=Crystal Palace appeal to CAS against Europa League demotion |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/ce8350jl5kgo |access-date=2025-07-23 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><!-- deliberately repeated references to support transclusion -->
|note_res_ECLPO=Since the winners of the [[2024–25 EFL Cup]], Newcastle United, qualified for the Champions League via league position, the spot reserved for the EFL Cup winners (Conference League play-off round) was initially passed to the 7th-placed team (Nottingham Forest). However due to [[Multi-club ownership (association football)|multi-club ownership]] rules, the winners of the FA Cup, Crystal Palace, were not permitted to enter the Europa League and entered the Conference League play-off round instead, with Nottingham Forest taking their place in the Europa League.<ref name="CRY_MultiClub">{{Cite web |date=2025-07-11 |title=Crystal Palace set to be replaced by Nottingham Forest in Europa League |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/ckg5260zzp2o |access-date=2025-07-11 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><!-- deliberately repeated references to support transclusion --> Crystal Palace appealed the decision but this was ultimately rejected.<ref name="CRY_Appeal">{{Cite web |date=2025-07-22 |title=Crystal Palace appeal to CAS against Europa League demotion |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/ce8350jl5kgo |access-date=2025-07-23 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><!-- deliberately repeated references to support transclusion -->
